================================================================================
Third-party components
================================================================================

This distribution links, at install time of the optional "postgres" extra
and in the published Docker image, the following weak-copyleft (LGPL-3.0)
components. They are dynamically linked / imported as separate works; SynthOrg
itself is not a derivative work of them. Their source is available from the
Python Package Index and the upstream project, and may be replaced or relinked
under the terms of the GNU Lesser General Public License, version 3.

  - psycopg (psycopg3)         LGPL-3.0-only   https://github.com/psycopg/psycopg
  - psycopg_pool               LGPL-3.0-only   https://github.com/psycopg/psycopg
  - psycopg_binary             LGPL-3.0-only   https://github.com/psycopg/psycopg

The full text of the GNU Lesser General Public License, version 3, is available
at https://www.gnu.org/licenses/lgpl-3.0.html.

Re-linking note (LGPL-3.0 section 4d0): to substitute a modified psycopg, build
the backend image with a replacement psycopg wheel installed in place of the
pinned version (the C extension `psycopg_binary` is an optional acceleration of
the pure-Python `psycopg`; the pure-Python package can be used standalone).

================================================================================
Deliberately excluded components
================================================================================

The following strong-copyleft components are intentionally NOT shipped, and a
gate (scripts/check_license_compat.py) keeps them out:

  - pymupdf / fitz (AGPL-3.0): excluded from all dependency tables.
  - golangci-lint (GPL-3.0):   used only as an external developer/CI binary,
                               never a Go module dependency of the CLI.
